{title: At The Cross}
{key: G}

{comment: Chorus}
At the [G]cross, at the [E7]cross
Where I [A]fir - [Bm]st  saw [A]the  [D]light
And the [Am]burden of my [D7]heart
Rolled [G]away, rolled [G7]away
It was [C]there by [Dbm]faith I re[G]ceived [B7]my    [E]sight
And [Am7]now I am [D]happy all the [G]day

{comment: Verse 1}
A[G]las and did my Savior bleed
And [C]did  [G]my   [Am]Sove - [G]reign [F]die?[Am][D]
Would [G]He devote that sacred head
For [C]such [Am]a     [D]worm as [G]I?[C]

{comment: Verse 2}
Was [G]it for crimes that I have done
He [C]groaned [G]u  -  [Am]pon   [G]the  [F]tree?[Am][D]
A[G]mazing pity, grace unknown
And [C]love [Am]be  -  [D]yond [G]deg - [C]ree
